{{!--
The srcset and src attributes of a picture stored by Ghost, in WebP: Ghost converts and resizes it on the
first request (/content/images/size/w600/format/webp/…), then serves the stored file. WebP rather than
AVIF: Ghost turns an animated GIF into an animated WebP but into a still AVIF, and encodes AVIF several
times slower (a first request can pass its 10 s limit on a small server). An SVG keeps its own format
(Ghost would rasterise it, then enlarge the bitmap). An image on another site is left alone by Ghost
(Unsplash: its own size and format parameters).
Parameters (named so, as a partial's parameters reach the partials it calls):
  image=...               the image (feature_image, cover_image…); the caller checks that there is one
  widths="s-m" | "s-m-l" | "m-l-xl"   srcset widths, theme image_sizes (package.json): s 300, m 600,
                          l 1000, w1400 1400 and xl 2000 (both in "m-l-xl")
  srcSize="s" | "m" | "l" | "xl"      size of the fallback src
Output: ` srcset="…" src="…"` (with the leading space); the caller writes sizes.
--}}
{{~#match image "~$" ".svg"~}}
  {{> "image/sources" imageFormat=false}}
{{~else match image "~$" ".SVG"~}}
  {{> "image/sources" imageFormat=false}}
{{~else~}}
  {{> "image/sources" imageFormat="webp"}}
{{~/match~}}
